{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And I will come down.</b> Because the heavens are more honored than the earth, and HaShem fills all with His glory—all—only because all decrees come from the heavens, therefore the word וארד; and further, because the rank of the angel is immense and Moses has no ability to ascend to the heavens, therefore the word וארד, to save my people:" "<b>And to bring him up.</b> Corresponding to וארד, for just as I dwell in a supreme place, so I will settle them in a place that is supreme over all the earth. And these are the words of the angel, and thus it is written: \"He makes him ride on the high places of the earth\" (Deuteronomy 32:13). Behold, they go out from a land where they are there in affliction to a good land. And he did not mention the Girgashite because he is the smallest of the seven. Now there is a fitting question: since the six nations are Canaan's sons, why did he mention the Canaanite? And the answer: because the whole land is called the land of Canaan, for it is the comprehensive name, which is the genus, and the Perizzite is Sidon, and the rest of the sons mentioned are few, and the verse encompasses all of them in the word הכנענים:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:19.740166782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}